## churches-register-2026-10.csv

- Overture Maps Foundation, places theme, release 2026-09-23.1 (s3://overturemaps-us-west-2/release/2026-09-23.1/theme=places/type=place/), read 2026-10-03. Overture places combine Meta, Microsoft and other open sources; see https://docs.overturemaps.org/guides/places/. Licence: CDLA Permissive 2.0 (places theme; per-record licences below).
- 2020 U.S. Religion Census state summary (https://www.usreligioncensus.org/sites/default/files/2023-06/2020_USRC_Summaries.xlsx, file dated 2023-06, downloaded 2026-10-03) for the cited congregation figures by state.
- US Census Bureau Vintage 2025 state population estimates (July 1, 2025), via FRED, for the per-100,000 rates.

Contains data from Overture Maps Foundation, licensed under CDLA Permissive 2.0 (https://cdla.dev/permissive-2-0/).

Per-record `sources` in the release (record-level entries only; Overture's own confidence calculation is left out). A place counts once under each licence or dataset it carries. Per-source licences checked on https://docs.overturemaps.org/attribution/ on 2026-10-03: Meta, Microsoft, PinMeTo, Krick, RenderSEO, DAC and BrightQuery under CDLA Permissive 2.0; Foursquare under Apache 2.0 (with its notice); AllThePlaces under CC0 1.0. No places source is listed under ODbL.

17,605 church locations carry a licence other than CDLA Permissive 2.0 (or none). Apache 2.0 (Foursquare) requires keeping Foursquare's copyright line, the licence and its notice file when the data is redistributed, so a list file with these rows must carry that notice, or leave the rows out. CC0 (AllThePlaces) needs no notice. No kept row is ODbL.

## dental-offices-2026-09.csv

1. **BLS QCEW, 2025 Q4, NAICS 621210 Offices of dentists**, open-data API https://data.bls.gov/cew/data/api/2025/4/industry/621210.csv, saved as `data/bls/qcew_2025q4_621210.csv`. Rows with `own_code` 5 (private). US: 138,795 establishments, which equals the sum of the 51 state rows. Government-owned offices add 14 nationally (own codes 2 and 3) and are ignored. Coverage: establishments with employees under state unemployment insurance.
2. **Census County Business Patterns 2023** (the latest year we could obtain), state file `cbp23st.zip`, from https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/cbp/datasets/2023/cbp23st.zip. census.gov and data.census.gov return HTTP 403 (Cloudflare) to this machine, and api.census.gov now requires a key. The file came from the Internet Archive capture of 2026-08-20 (https://web.archive.org/web/20260820164306id_/https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/cbp/datasets/2023/cbp23st.zip) and is saved in `data/census/`. `naics`=621210, `lfo`='-': 135,665 establishments in the 50 states + DC, 51,142 of them with fewer than 5 employees. We found no archived CBP 2024 file and couldn't confirm whether it is published.
3. **Census Nonemployer Statistics 2024**, state file `nonemp24st.zip`, https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/nonemployer-statistics/datasets/2024/historical-datasets/nonemp24st.zip, via the Internet Archive capture of 2026-09-29. The state file goes down to NAICS 4-digit only. 6212 (Offices of dentists) contains only 621210, so it is the same industry. `LFO`='-': 57,079 nonemployer firms in the 50 states + DC (2023 file: 54,452). These are businesses with no paid employees, mostly sole proprietors. We could not measure how many run their own office, so they are shown for context and excluded from the estimate.
4. **CMS NPPES, file dated 2026-09-14** (see `dentists-stats-2026-09.md`), with its 216,788 candidate practice locations (normalized street address + ZIP5).
5. **CMS Medicare Part D Prescribers by Provider, data year 2024.** API id `14d8e8a9-7e9b-4370-a044-bf97c46b4b44`. We used the full NPI list, plus the practice addresses of the 140,007 rows with a dental prescriber type ("Dentist", "Oral Surgery (Dentist only)", "Maxillofacial Surgery", "Oral & Maxillofacial Surgery"). The addresses were normalized the same way as NPPES.
6. **Overture Maps places, release 2026-09-23.1** (latest on `s3://overturemaps-us-west-2/release/` on 2026-09-29), 16 GeoParquet files of about 11 GB, scanned remotely with DuckDB httpfs in 450 seconds. This release has no `categories` column. Categories are in `taxonomy.primary` and `taxonomy.hierarchy`. The dental categories found: `dental_clinic` 101,947; `general_dentistry` 44,296; `orthodontics` 15,298; `pediatric_dentistry` 10,710; `cosmetic_dentistry` 9,189; `oral_and_maxillofacial_surgery` 8,316; `endodontics` 4,601; `periodontics` 3,218; `prosthodontics` 814; `dental_hygiene` 100. That totals 198,489 US rows. Excluded as non-offices: `b2b_dental_lab`, `dental_supply_store`, `dentistry_school`, `student_union`, `mobile_dent_repair`. States come from `addresses[1].region`, which holds two-letter codes (21 rows had none).
7. Population is not used here.

Overture credit (same release; wording from church/veterinary provenance):
Contains data from Overture Maps Foundation, licensed under CDLA Permissive 2.0 (https://cdla.dev/permissive-2-0/).

