## dentists-stats-2026-09.csv

1. **CMS NPPES Data Dissemination V.2, file dated 2026-09-14** (`NPPES_Data_Dissemination_September_2026_V2.zip`, SHA-256 `6573e0d1…3cec4`), from https://download.cms.gov/nppes/NPI_Files.html, downloaded 2026-09-20. Extraction and clustering are documented in [the dental feasibility report](../../research/2026-09-20-dental-feasibility/170724Z/report.md) (scripts `01_extract_dental.py` and `02_analyze.py` in that folder). The stats script reads the derived files `data/nppes/derived/core.parquet`, `loc2.parquet`, `spec.parquet` and `clusters.parquet` (not in Git; `data/` is ignored).
2. **CMS Medicare Part D Prescribers - by Provider, data year 2024.** Catalog entry "Medicare Part D Prescribers - by Provider : 2024-12-03", modified 2026-08-03 (https://data.cms.gov/data.json). API: https://data.cms.gov/data-api/v1/dataset/14d8e8a9-7e9b-4370-a044-bf97c46b4b44/data. All 1,416,883 rows were paged on 2026-09-29 with four columns (NPI, prescriber type, state, total claims). Every NPI is kept whatever its prescriber type, and the join to dental NPIs is by NPI. 138,329 of our dentist NPIs appear (131,021 typed "Dentist", 5,625 "Oral Surgery (Dentist only)", the rest in other types). CMS suppresses prescribers with fewer than 11 claims in the year. 2024 is the latest data year in the catalog on 2026-09-29.
3. **US Census Bureau, Vintage 2025 population estimates, resident population on July 1, 2025** (release "Annual Estimates of the Population for the U.S. and States, and for Puerto Rico", published 2026-01-27). Census's own file `NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv` (https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/popest/datasets/2020-2025/state/totals/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv) and table page returned HTTP 403 (Cloudflare block) from this machine on 2026-09-29. The same Census series was taken from FRED, series `<ST>POP` (e.g. https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/TXPOP; "Source: U.S. Census Bureau", thousands of persons with three decimals, i.e. exact persons; FRED last updated 2026-03-03), retrieved 2026-09-29 and saved to `data/census/fred_state_pop_v2025.csv`. Check: the Texas 2024 to 2025 change in the FRED data is 391,243, the same figure as the Census Vintage 2025 press release. The 50 states + DC sum to 341,784,857. **Verified 2026-09-29:** all 51 values match `POPESTIMATE2025` in the official `NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv`, taken from the Internet Archive capture of 2026-08-19 (https://web.archive.org/web/20260819082738id_/https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/popest/datasets/2020-2025/state/totals/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv) and saved to `data/census/`. The published page rounds our computed counts (Žan's rule of 2026-09-29), while this CSV keeps exact values.
4. External benchmarks quoted on the page (not in the CSV):
   - ADA Health Policy Institute, "Dentist Workforce", https://www.ada.org/resources/research/health-policy-institute/dentist-workforce, accessed 2026-09-29: 205,088 professionally active dentists as of 2025; 60.0 per 100,000 population; 21.2% in an ADA-recognized specialty area.
   - BLS OEWS, May 2025, national, all industries, employment (BLS public API, 2026-09-29): Dentists 29-1020 = 141,610 (series OEUN000000000000029102001); General 29-1021 = 124,390; Oral and Maxillofacial Surgeons 29-1022 = 4,910; Orthodontists 29-1023 = 6,210; Prosthodontists 29-1024 = 870; All Other Specialists 29-1029 = 5,230. OEWS excludes the self-employed.
   - BLS QCEW, NAICS 621210 Offices of dentists, US, private, number of establishments (series ENUUS000205621210, BLS public API, 2026-09-29): 138,795 in Q4 2025; 138,982 in Q1 2026 (preliminary).

License of the published CSV: CC BY 4.0 (attribution: nodilist.com, from CMS and US Census Bureau data).

